
. do example.do

. * nwcommands tutorial 13: testing hypotheses about networks
. * Requires the core nwcommands.
. 
. * 1. Is a statistic unusual for a network of this size and density? (CUG test)
. nwwebuse florentine, nwclear

. nwsummarize flomarriage
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  flomarriage
   Network id:  2
   Directed: false
   Valued: false
   Two-mode: false
   Nodes: 16
   Selfloop: false
   Edges: 20
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  1
   Density:  .167
   Mean degree:  2.50
   Temporal: false

. nwcug flomarriage, stat(nwtriads) rname(transitivity) reps(500) seed(12345)

Conditional uniform graph test                   Number of draws =        500
Network: flomarriage                             Condition       =    density
Statistic: r(transitivity) after nwtriads flomarriage

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |  Observed Null mean   Null sd  P >= obs  P <= obs Two-sided
-------------+-------------------------------------------------------------
transitivity |  .1914894  .1487523  .0819702    0.3174    0.6966    0.6347
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

. nwcug flomarriage, stat(nwcomponents, generate(cc) replace silent) rname(components) reps(500) see
> d(12345)

Conditional uniform graph test                   Number of draws =        500
Network: flomarriage                             Condition       =    density
Statistic: r(components) after nwcomponents flomarriage, generate(cc) replace silent

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |  Observed Null mean   Null sd  P >= obs  P <= obs Two-sided
-------------+-------------------------------------------------------------
  components |         2     1.986  .8118634    0.7066    0.7625    1.0000
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. * 2. Is one network related to another? (QAP correlation)
. nwwebuse glasgow, nwclear

. nwcorrelate glasgow1 glasgow2

Network correlation
Network 1: glasgow1
Network 2: glasgow2

-------------
 Correlation
-------------
   .47324572
-------------

. nwcorrelate glasgow1 glasgow2, permutations(500)

Network correlation                              Permutations    =        500
Network 1: glasgow1
Network 2: glasgow2

----------------------------------------------------------
 Correlation     P-value   [95% permutation interval]
----------------------------------------------------------
   .47324572      0.0040      -.03985912   .04260416
----------------------------------------------------------

. 
. * 3. Does a covariate explain ties? (QAP regression)
. nwqap glasgow2 glasgow1 smoke1 sport1



Multiple Regression Quadratic Assignment Procedure

  Estimation            =  QAP
  Regression            =  logit
  Permutations          =  500
  Number of vertices    =  50
  Number of arcs        =  116

-------------------------------------------------
              glasgow2 |      Coef.    P-value
-----------------------+-------------------------
              glasgow1 |      3.653     .002
           same_smoke1 |       .514     .044
           same_sport1 |       .217     .345
                 _cons |     -4.125
-------------------------------------------------


. 
. * 4. The CUG test again, holding every family's number of marriages fixed
. nwwebuse florentine, nwclear

. nwcug flomarriage, stat(nwtriads) rname(transitivity) condition(degrees) reps(500) seed(12345)

Conditional uniform graph test                   Number of draws =        500
Network: flomarriage                             Condition       =    degrees
Statistic: r(transitivity) after nwtriads flomarriage

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |  Observed Null mean   Null sd  P >= obs  P <= obs Two-sided
-------------+-------------------------------------------------------------
transitivity |  .1914894  .1604681  .0796446    0.4810    0.7984    0.9621
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

